All agencies involved in responding to violence against women and their children cases shall be required to undergo education and training to acquaint them with the:
a) Nature, extent and causes of VAWC;
b) Legal rights of, and remedies available to, victim-survivors of VAWC;
c) Services and facilities available to victim-survivors;
d) Legal duties of police officers in the arrest of perpetrators and protection and assistance to victim-survivors; and
e) Techniques for handling incidents of VAWC that minimize the likelihood of injury to the officer and promote the safety of the victim-survivor.
The PNP, in coordination with LGUs, shall establish an education and training program for police officers and barangay officials to enable them to properly handle cases of violence against women and their children.

